# Credentials — never commit
config.py

# trades.csv used to be listed here as "local-only personal data" — but that
# meant load_trades() found nothing on every GitHub Actions checkout (fresh
# clone, file never committed), so CI operated on an empty ledger every run:
# added Friday's practice trades, emailed them, then threw them away when the
# job ended. Nothing ever carried forward. Now tracked and committed by CI
# alongside scan_history.csv, exactly like the rest of the scan state — this
# repo is private, so real position data in git history is an accepted risk
# the user explicitly signed off on (2026-09-04).

# Generated outputs (rebuilt on each run)
digest_preview.html
universe_cache.json
tracker.html
notify.log
# last_scan.json tracked intentionally — CI commits it for GitHub Pages + email matrix

